    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 all three identifiers now mix in a fixed `\"V2\"` tag, so every value changes and no version-1 value recurs:\n- New `common/IdentityVersion.java` holds the single source of truth: `TAG = \"V2\"`, `API_VERSION = 2`, `SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`.\n- `MemberId.base` \u2014 the `HASH8` input now mixes `\"V2\" + region` into the digest. The **visible `<REGION>` prefix stays the plain region** (`NSW`), so `MemberId.regionOf`/`fiscalYearLabel` parsing and the locality read-back are unaffected.\n- `OwnerHousehold.id` \u2014 `householdId` digest now prefixed with the `V2` tag (household grouping preserved: still deterministic from last name + postcode).\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.of` \u2014 `identityKey` digest now prefixed with the `V2` tag (duplicate detection preserved: both sides computed identically).\n\n**Locality/timezone/segment stay tag-free** \u2014 because the memberId's region prefix remains plain, `locality` is still `\"NSW\"`, `timezone` unchanged, and `OwnerSegment` derives `METRO`/`REGIONAL` from the plain region. The `V2` tag lives only inside the hashed identifiers.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerated DTOs + `OwnerMapper`):\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`.\n- New nested `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`; those three removed from the top level.\n- Mapper populates `apiVersion` and builds the nested `identity` object; `fiscalYear` stays top-level.\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema version 2** (`OwnerCreatedEvent` + `AuditOwnerCreated`):\n- Added `schemaVersion: 2` and a `segment` field recomputed via `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`.\n- Verified emitted line: `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSW27971AFBC40\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"segment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` \u2014 segment region is plain `NSW`, no tag leak.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.",
