    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here's the complete ordered breakdown.\n\n## Validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`\n\nThe whole pipeline runs inside a **single write transaction** (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), committing once at the end. Steps run in this order:\n\n### 0. Authorization (endpoint guard)\n- **`hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`** \u2014 the `composition.authorize` SpEL guards the whole file; a caller lacking the role is rejected (401/403 via the `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler) before any step runs.\n\n### 1. Idempotency check \u2014 `CheckIdempotentCreate`\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it (null if absent).\n- **Side-effect / short-circuit:** if the key was already recorded *and* its owner still exists, it republishes that original owner and branches to `respondExisting` \u2192 responds **200** with the original owner, creating no duplicate. Otherwise continues.\n\n### 2. Field validation & normalization \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (the one step that reads `@RequestBody`)\nOrder of checks matters here:\n- Normalizes address first: trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST/RD/AVE` \u2192 `STREET/ROAD/AVENUE`. If `addressLine1` is present, the structured form is composed into `address` (line1 + optional line2); otherwise the flat `address` is used.\n- **Required-field check** (after normalization): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 else **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`) naming all missing fields.\n- **Telephone normalization** to E.164 (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`): strips separators; keeps explicit `+`, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; must be 8\u201315 digits; recognized country codes must have exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidOwnerTelephoneException`). Normalized value is stored back on the body.\n- **Email normalization** (`OwnerEmail.normalize`), only if email present: must match the syntactic pattern \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidOwnerEmailException`); lower-cased; domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 else **400** (`DisposableOwnerEmailException`). Stored lower-cased.\n- **Postcode validation** (`OwnerPostcode.validate`), only if present: must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in range \u2192 else **400** (`InvalidOwnerPostcodeException`).\n- **Future registration date check:** if `registrationDate` supplied and after the server date \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n- Publishes the validated/normalized body.\n\n### 3. Duplicate-identity check \u2014 `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`\n- Computes the identityKey = SHA-256 over normalized telephone | lower email | Soundex(lastName). If it equals any existing **non-deleted** owner's \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`). This is the only hard duplicate block; soft-deleted owners don't block.\n\n### 4. City-capacity check \u2014 `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- If the request's city already holds \u2265 **50** owners \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`). (New owner not yet counted.)\n\n### 5. Daily-create-limit check \u2014 `EnsureDailyCreateLimit`\n- Effective registration date (supplied else today) is rolled forward to a business day; if \u2265 **100** owners already carry that adjusted date \u2192 **429** (`DailyCreateLimitException`).\n\n### 6. Build entity \u2014 `BuildOwner`\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to the business-day-adjusted effective date.\n\n### 7. Assign memberId \u2014 `AssignOwnerMemberId`\n- Sets `memberId = <REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from postcode, 2-digit fiscal year, first 8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName), Luhn check digit). On collision with an existing memberId, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 for uniqueness.\n\n### 8. Assign household \u2014 `AssignOwnerHousehold`\n- Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(normalizedLastName | postcode); null when no postcode.\n\n### 9. Assign namesake count \u2014 `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = number of **existing** owners (before this create) with the same firstName+lastName, case-insensitively.\n\n### 10. Persist \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- **Saves the owner to the repository** (assigns the id). A DB constraint violation escalates as `DataIntegrityViolationException` (has its own handler).\n\n### 11. Record idempotency \u2014 `RecordIdempotentCreate`\n- If a key was supplied, **records** `key \u2192 owner.id` in the idempotency store (so a later repeat returns this owner). No-op when no key.\n\n### 12. Audit \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Emits two AUDIT log lines:** a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) and a compact JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (monotonic `seq`, schemaVersion 2, id, memberId, level, segment).\n\n### 13. Welcome notification \u2014 `NotifyWelcome`\n- **Emits a NOTIFY log line** (owner id + memberId) to enqueue a welcome notification.\n\nThe remaining steps compute **transient, non-persisted flags** on the returned owner (each counting the just-saved owner, so a later GET recomputes the same value):\n\n### 14. `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning`\n- `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > **80** owners share this registration day.\n\n### 15. `AssignOwnerCapacityWarning`\n- `capacityWarning = true` if the city now holds **40\u201349** owners.\n\n### 16. `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`\n- `householdSize` = owners sharing the householdId (incl. this one); 1 if no household. Drives the GOLD tier (3+).\n\n### 17. `AssignOwnerMembershipLevel`\n- `membershipLevel` = the owner's level, **capped** at one above the max level among other household members (uncapped if no other members).\n\n### 18. `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`\n- `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` = soft match: same postcode + Soundex(lastName) as an existing non-deleted, non-hard-duplicate owner (earliest/lowest id). False when no postcode.\n\n### 19. `AssignOwnerRiskFlag`\n- `riskFlag = true` if any of: it's a possible duplicate, its email domain is disposable-*adjacent* (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `x.mailinator.com`), or its city holds \u2265 **40** owners.\n\n### 20. Respond \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- Sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the owner DTO body.\n\n---\n\n**Note on ordering rationale baked into the pipeline:** validation precedes duplicate/capacity/limit checks (so a bad body is 400, not masked); those precede build/save; and all the flag-assignment side-effects run *after* save specifically so their counts include the new owner and match what a later GET recomputes."
